      "id": 1,
      "text": "Margarettsville got its name in 1836 when a Seaboard railroad official named the settlement after local resident Margaret Jordan, adding “tsville” for a unique twist.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/margarettsville_north_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened the same year, cementing Margarettsville’s status as a formal community in 1836.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margarettsville%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s roots trace back to the early 1700s when Virginia migrants settled the fertile lands along the Meherrin River, making it one of Northampton County’s first European communities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
